# Line endings for the files the BUILD reads, which is not the same set as the
# files a person reads.
#
# Everything that compiles this kernel runs inside WSL, where a carriage return
# is a character rather than whitespace.  This repository is developed with
# core.autocrlf on, so a fresh clone -- or, as it happened here, a second
# worktree checked out to verify a commit -- gets CRLF in every text file, and
# then "#!/bin/sh\r" names an interpreter that does not exist.  The build dies
# with "tools/gen_ksyms.sh: not found" pointing at a file that is right there,
# which is a diagnosis nobody would arrive at from the message.
#
# So the shell scripts, the makefiles and the python helpers are pinned to LF
# regardless of what the checkout would otherwise do.  PowerShell is run by
# Windows and is deliberately left alone.
*.sh		text eol=lf
*.py		text eol=lf
*.mk		text eol=lf
Makefile	text eol=lf
